+# Implementation notes
+
+## 001 Existing membership and projection-barrier inspection
+
+- Membership has two Commanded applications per ADR 0007:
+  - `Memba.Membership.App` / `Memba.Membership.Router` own Membership commands,
+    aggregates, events, and projections.
+  - `Memba.Messaging.App` / `Memba.Messaging.Router` own Messaging commands,
+    aggregates, events, and projections.
+- `Memba.Membership.Club` currently owns club identity and club-scoped roles:
+  - state fields: `club_id`, `name`, `slug`, `roles`, `role_keys`,
+    `role_permissions`, and `role_assignments`;
+  - `CreateClub` emits `ClubCreated`, the deterministic Admin `ClubRoleDefined`,
+    and `ClubRolePermissionGranted` for `club.manage_members`;
+  - `AssignMemberRole` / `RemoveMemberRole` dispatch to the Club aggregate and
+    validate role existence, duplicate assignment/removal, and person/membership
+    identity consistency inside Club state.
+- Membership lifecycle currently lives in `Memba.Membership.Membership`:
+  - `AddMember` emits `MemberAdded` with `membership_id`, `club_id`, and
+    `person_id`;
+  - `RemoveMember` emits `MemberRemoved` with only `membership_id`;
+  - the aggregate tracks current `active` state but does not own role or group
+    state.
+- Public Membership application services enforce cross-aggregate/query rules:
+  - `add_member/2` prevents duplicate active `{club_id, person_id}` memberships
+    before dispatch;
+  - Admin-specific entry points derive `Roles.membership_administrator_role_id/1`;
+  - role assignment/removal entry points authorize via projected
+    `club.manage_members`, ensure the target membership is active, and preserve the
+    last-Admin invariant before dispatching Club role commands.
+- ID conventions are centralized in `Memba.ID`:
+  - caller-generated typed IDs use `ID.generate/1`;
+  - deterministic typed IDs use `ID.deterministic/2`;
+  - adding groups will require a new typed ID prefix/type before deterministic
+    Everyone/Admin group IDs can be defined.
+- Existing strong projectors use `Commanded.Projections.Ecto` with stable string
+  names and `consistency: :strong`.
+  - Membership role projection toggles current-state rows for role assignments and
+    responds to `MemberRemoved` by deactivating assignments and deleting flattened
+    permissions.
+  - Projection table reset coverage is configured in
+    `config :memba, :event_sourced_projection_tables`.
+- `Memba.EventSourcedCase.rebuild_event_sourced_projections!/0` stops configured
+  projectors, truncates configured projection tables, resets Commanded
+  subscriptions and EventStore subscription checkpoints, then restarts the same
+  projectors.
+- `Memba.ProjectionBarrier` waits for selected projector names in
+  `projection_versions` to reach the current or supplied EventStore checkpoint;
+  replay-parity work will need to add future group/access projectors to the
+  EventSourcedCase projector list and projection table config before awaiting them.
